amdxdna drives the neural processing unit (NPU) of AMD Ryzen AI
processors, an array of AI Engine tiles (XDNA and XDNA 2) that runs
machine learning workloads at low power.  It is the Linux amdxdna
driver from the accel subsystem, ported to FreeBSD on top of drm-kmod
and LinuxKPI.  It exposes /dev/accel/accel0 for AMD's XRT runtime
(devel/xrt).

On FreeBSD it runs in carveout mode: NPU buffers come from one
physically contiguous region reserved at attach, because FreeBSD has no
IOMMU shared virtual addressing.
